+## Failure semantics
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws, the orchestrator passes the same session and error to `onError`, then calls `afterSession`, then rejects its caller with the original error. `afterSession` must therefore tolerate a partially initialized session: it may assume `beforeSession` was entered, but cannot assume that it completed or that any later stage of the turn began. ([validated by: reports and cleans up a beforeSession failure before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionFailure.acceptance.test.ts#L6))
